1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,012
Imagine walking into the third set of a grueling
90-minute padel match feeling just

2
00:00:06,012 --> 00:00:08,335
as explosive as the opening game.

3
00:00:08,685 --> 00:00:11,667
Your legs feel light, your
split-step is sharp,

4
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,145
and while your opponents are bent
over gasping for air,

5
00:00:15,145 --> 00:00:17,133
you are ready to attack the net.

6
00:00:17,483 --> 00:00:21,581
Today, I will show you why
traditional cardio fails in padel,

7
00:00:21,581 --> 00:00:25,547
and the exact court science to never
get tired on the glass.

8
00:00:25,897 --> 00:00:30,100
Most players train for padel like
it is a 5k road race.

9
00:00:30,449 --> 00:00:34,205
They go for long, steady jogs, but
when match day comes,

10
00:00:34,205 --> 00:00:37,830
their legs feel like concrete
blocks by the second set.

11
00:00:38,181 --> 00:00:44,457
Padel is not a marathon; it is an intermittent
combat sport played inside a 10 by 20

12
00:00:44,457 --> 00:00:45,712
meter glass cage.

13
00:00:46,061 --> 00:00:49,934
An average rally lasts only
6 to 12 seconds,

14
00:00:49,934 --> 00:00:53,549
separated by 15 to 25 seconds of recovery.

15
00:00:53,899 --> 00:00:57,479
In a full match, you cover up
to 4,000 meters,

16
00:00:57,479 --> 00:01:03,115
but you also execute over 400 violent
braking stops and direction changes.

17
00:01:03,465 --> 00:01:08,777
To never get tired, you need 4 specific
engines: the metabolic recharger,

18
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:14,089
eccentric brake pads, tactical court
economy, and the between-point reset.

19
00:01:14,439 --> 00:01:17,997
When you scramble for an
explosive ball off the glass,

20
00:01:17,997 --> 00:01:20,455
your body relies on a two-part engine.

21
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:24,281
The first 6 to 8 seconds of
every sprint, lunge,

22
00:01:24,281 --> 00:01:30,170
and smash are powered by pure phosphocreatine
stored directly in your muscle cells.

23
00:01:30,521 --> 00:01:36,452
This is your alactic battery: instant explosive
power with zero lactic acid buildup.

24
00:01:36,801 --> 00:01:42,130
When a point drags past 15 seconds, your
anaerobic glycolysis kicks in,

25
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:46,422
producing burning hydrogen ions and
spiking blood lactate.

26
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:49,930
This is where your aerobic
system enters the game.

27
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:55,995
Your aerobic ceiling does not power the sprint;
it functions as the rapid recharger

28
00:01:55,995 --> 00:01:58,920
during the 15 to 20 seconds
between points.

29
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:04,665
Think of a hybrid sports car: the electric
battery delivers instant torque off the

30
00:02:04,665 --> 00:02:10,189
line, while the internal generator recharges the
battery the second you lift off the

31
00:02:10,189 --> 00:02:10,449
gas.

32
00:02:10,799 --> 00:02:13,243
If your aerobic generator is small,

33
00:02:13,243 --> 00:02:17,860
your explosive battery only recharges
halfway before the next serve.

34
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:23,562
To train this, ditch steady-state jogging and
use Padel Court Shuttles: sprint from

35
00:02:23,562 --> 00:02:27,767
the baseline to the net, backpedal, and
shuffle to the side glass.

36
00:02:28,117 --> 00:02:31,338
Perform 8 to 10 seconds of all-out effort,

37
00:02:31,338 --> 00:02:35,008
followed by 20 to 25 seconds of
walking recovery.

38
00:02:35,358 --> 00:02:41,168
Complete 2 blocks of 6 to 8 reps, resting 3
minutes between blocks once or twice a

39
00:02:41,168 --> 00:02:44,318
week; beginners start with 1
block in week 1.

40
00:02:44,668 --> 00:02:48,765
Have you ever noticed that your lungs
feel fine in the third set,

41
00:02:48,765 --> 00:02:51,559
but your thighs and calves
refuse to explode?

42
00:02:51,909 --> 00:02:57,222
That heaviness is not a lack of cardio; it
is the accumulation of eccentric

43
00:02:57,222 --> 00:02:58,480
deceleration debt.

44
00:02:58,829 --> 00:03:01,624
Unlike tennis or football on open turf,

45
00:03:01,624 --> 00:03:07,213
padel requires hundreds of sudden braking
stops on sand-dressed artificial turf.

46
00:03:07,563 --> 00:03:13,050
Every time you sprint forward and slam the
brakes, your quadriceps, hamstrings,

47
00:03:13,050 --> 00:03:16,480
and calves undergo violent
eccentric contractions.

48
00:03:16,831 --> 00:03:21,784
Your muscles are forced to lengthen under
immense load to absorb your forward

49
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:22,356
momentum.

50
00:03:22,706 --> 00:03:29,146
Over 90 minutes, absorbing 400 braking stops
causes microscopic structural damage to

51
00:03:29,146 --> 00:03:33,010
muscle fibers, degrading your
neuromuscular firing.

52
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:38,151
Think of the brake pads on a race car: the
gas tank may still have fuel,

53
00:03:38,151 --> 00:03:42,811
but once the brake pads wear down to bare
metal, the car cannot corner.

54
00:03:43,161 --> 00:03:45,923
To build indestructible brake pads,

55
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:52,214
train tempo Eccentric Box Step-Downs: start on
a low 15-centimeter step and lower

56
00:03:52,214 --> 00:03:55,897
your heel to the floor over 3
to 4 slow seconds.

57
00:03:56,247 --> 00:04:01,230
Do 3 sets of 8 to 10 reps per leg twice
a week; if your knees hurt,

58
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:05,847
substitute isometric wall sits under a
physio's guidance first.

59
00:04:06,197 --> 00:04:11,727
Pair this with Loaded Deficit Calf Raises:
start with two legs on flat ground,

60
00:04:11,727 --> 00:04:17,397
then progress to single-leg deficit raises
lowering for 3 seconds below the step.

61
00:04:17,747 --> 00:04:23,931
Do 3 sets of 12 to 15 reps to protect your
Achilles tendons from repetitive braking

62
00:04:23,931 --> 00:04:24,446
shocks.

63
00:04:24,795 --> 00:04:30,014
Here is a shocking stat from match tracking:
elite padel players sustain lower

64
00:04:30,014 --> 00:04:35,035
average heart rates than club amateurs,
despite hitting with far more power.

65
00:04:35,385 --> 00:04:40,581
Amateur players waste up to 30 percent of their
court movement running frantically

66
00:04:40,581 --> 00:04:43,022
in no-man's land near the service line.

67
00:04:43,373 --> 00:04:46,594
Elite stamina is about
positional geometry.

68
00:04:46,944 --> 00:04:51,728
First, anchor your base in the
defensive sweet spot: exactly 0.

69
00:04:51,728 --> 00:04:56,736
8 meters behind the service line and 1
meter in from the side glass.

70
00:04:57,086 --> 00:05:02,300
From this home base, you can cover the vast
majority of opponent attacking balls

71
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,617
with just one or two balanced steps.

72
00:05:04,967 --> 00:05:08,646
Second, move with your partner as
a synchronized unit,

73
00:05:08,646 --> 00:05:11,388
connected by an invisible 3-meter string.

74
00:05:11,738 --> 00:05:15,249
When your partner slides wide to
dig out a corner ball,

75
00:05:15,249 --> 00:05:19,951
you slide into the middle channel, cutting
wasted recovery sprints in half.

76
00:05:20,301 --> 00:05:23,677
Third, when you are under
suffocating pressure,

77
00:05:23,677 --> 00:05:28,600
use padel's ultimate biological timeout:
the high defensive reset lob.

78
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:36,015
A properly lofted lob reaches 5 to 8 meters
high and hangs in the air for 3.

79
00:05:36,015 --> 00:05:36,749
5 to 4.

80
00:05:36,749 --> 00:05:37,483
5 seconds.

81
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:43,194
Those 4 seconds act like an aerial parachute:
they break the opponents' attack,

82
00:05:43,194 --> 00:05:48,622
force them to retreat, and give you 4 seconds
of live in-point recovery to lower

83
00:05:48,622 --> 00:05:49,694
your heart rate.

84
00:05:50,045 --> 00:05:55,080
Practice the 4-Second Lob drill: scoop
deep lobs off the back glass,

85
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:59,167
timing each shot with a stopwatch
to ensure at least 3.

86
00:05:59,167 --> 00:06:00,626
5 seconds of airtime.

87
00:06:00,976 --> 00:06:06,309
The official rules of padel give you up to 20
seconds between consecutive points.

88
00:06:06,659 --> 00:06:11,892
How you spend those 20 seconds determines
whether your heart rate spikes into the

89
00:06:11,892 --> 00:06:13,934
red zone or drops into recovery.

90
00:06:14,284 --> 00:06:19,648
When amateurs finish a hard rally, they drop
their head, gasp through an open mouth,

91
00:06:19,648 --> 00:06:21,793
and rush to pick up the next ball.

92
00:06:22,143 --> 00:06:27,464
Rapid mouth panting prolongs sympathetic
fight-or-flight adrenaline,

93
00:06:27,464 --> 00:06:31,551
keeping your heart racing above
175 beats per minute.

94
00:06:31,901 --> 00:06:38,102
Elite competitors use a structured 15-second pit
stop routine to trigger their vagus

95
00:06:38,102 --> 00:06:40,072
nerve and slow their pulse.

96
00:06:40,422 --> 00:06:44,760
In the first 3 seconds after the point,
turn your back to the net,

97
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,867
drop your racket head, and
physically disengage.

98
00:06:48,217 --> 00:06:53,278
From second 4 to 12, stand tall with hands
on hips to expand your ribs,

99
00:06:53,278 --> 00:06:56,581
inhale slowly through your
nose for 4 seconds,

100
00:06:56,581 --> 00:07:00,377
and exhale smoothly through
pursed lips for 6 seconds.

101
00:07:00,727 --> 00:07:05,293
Just two cycles of slow breathing
activate your parasympathetic brake,

102
00:07:05,293 --> 00:07:09,538
rapidly pulling your heart rate down
before the next point starts.

103
00:07:09,888 --> 00:07:13,004
In the final 5 seconds, turn
back to the court,

104
00:07:13,004 --> 00:07:17,483
give your partner a quick tactical cue,
and assume your ready stance.

105
00:07:17,833 --> 00:07:23,222
Never rush to serve when your heart is pounding;
use 12 to 15 seconds of your legal

106
00:07:23,222 --> 00:07:26,302
window to start every point
with a fresh engine.

107
00:07:26,652 --> 00:07:29,660
To lock this stamina
framework into your game,

108
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:32,412
follow this balanced 3-day
weekly protocol.

109
00:07:32,762 --> 00:07:38,789
On Tuesday, complete your 25-minute Court
Shuttle session: 2 blocks of 8 reps of

110
00:07:38,789 --> 00:07:42,063
10-second sprints with
20-second recoveries.

111
00:07:42,413 --> 00:07:48,761
On Thursday, dedicate 35 minutes to Eccentric
Strength: Tempo Box Step-Downs and

112
00:07:48,761 --> 00:07:50,328
Deficit Calf Raises.

113
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:53,567
On Saturday, take the court
for match play,

114
00:07:53,567 --> 00:07:58,886
anchoring in the defensive sweet spot and
practicing the 15-second between-point

115
00:07:58,886 --> 00:07:59,937
breathing reset.

116
00:08:00,287 --> 00:08:06,111
Always complete an 8-minute dynamic warm-up
with lateral shuffles and submaximal

117
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:08,628
deceleration brakes before playing.

118
00:08:08,978 --> 00:08:15,046
Remember hydration: covered glass courts
create greenhouse humidity where sweat

119
00:08:15,046 --> 00:08:16,563
rates reach 1 to 1.

120
00:08:16,563 --> 00:08:22,631
5 liters per hour, so drink 500 milliliters
with electrolytes every hour of play.

121
00:08:22,981 --> 00:08:27,604
If you ever feel a sudden sharp snap or
kick in the back of your heel,

122
00:08:27,604 --> 00:08:33,008
stop immediately and seek emergency medical
evaluation for an Achilles tendon tear.

123
00:08:33,358 --> 00:08:38,137
Never getting tired in padel is not about
running endless road miles.

124
00:08:38,487 --> 00:08:43,406
Recharge your explosive battery,
bulletproof your eccentric brake pads,

125
00:08:43,406 --> 00:08:47,505
command the sweet spot, and master
the between-point reset.

126
00:08:47,505 --> 00:08:48,940
See you on the court.
